    {
      "name": "Thunderstorm",
      "type": "feature",
      "system": {
        "featureForm": "action",
        "description": "<p><strong>Spend a Fear</strong> to have a torrential downpour soak the land. Each PC must either seek shelter from the storm or collect rainwater. Each PC who seeks shelter marks a Stress. The PCs who collect rainwater make a group action roll.</p><ul><li><p>On a success with Hope, add <strong>1d4</strong> tokens to the Water Supply.</p></li><li><p>On a success with Fear, add 1 token to the Water Supply.</p></li><li><p>On a failure with Hope, each PC who took part in the group action roll marks a Stress.</p></li><li><p>On a failure with Fear, each PC who took part in the group action roll marks a Stress, and the PC who rolled the lowest takes <strong>2d8+4</strong> physical damage from the storm.</p></li></ul><section id=\"secret-zav64YaMGRmiq3pt\" class=\"secret\"><p>How does the storm look to the heroes as it rolls in from miles away? Is the storm natural or unnatural? How can you tell?</p></section>",
        "attribution": {},
        "gmNotes": "",
